  "articleBodyHtml": "<h2>Initial Experimentation with Settings</h2>\n<p>The speaker is experimenting with turning off various settings and acknowledges the resulting instability. They mention turning off the &#x27;Komaru wa&#x27; feature and restarting the game, noting that the experience is &#x27;a little rough.&#x27;</p>\n<p>Despite the instability, the speaker believes the changes will be acceptable for the actual release, stating, &#x27;I feel like it will be okay for the actual release.&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Concerns About Frequent Restarts</h2>\n<p>The speaker expresses concern about the need for frequent restarts due to the changes made. They ask, &#x27;Does this mean that every time I play this on this PC, like, I would have to restart every once in a while?&#x27; and note that this is &#x27;not ideal.&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Consideration of Further Adjustments</h2>\n<p>The speaker is considering further adjustments to the settings, as indicated by phrases like &#x27;Mmm...&#x27; and &#x27;I guess I could...&#x27; suggesting they are contemplating additional changes.</p>\n<h2>Acknowledgment of Potential Limitations</h2>\n<p>The speaker acknowledges that the issue might not be resolved by the current changes, stating, &#x27;Really, it&#x27;s not fixed by turning off compatibility settings and verifying game files.&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Performance Issues and Hardware Considerations</h2>\n<p>The speaker is initially experiencing performance issues with the game and is considering upgrading their hardware, specifically mentioning the possibility of upgrading RAM and storage.</p>\n<p>The game is consistently running at 100% CPU usage, and the speaker is investigating the cause, suspecting factors like surface quality or render distance.</p>\n<p>The speaker confirms that the game was previously functioning correctly during testing, but is now experiencing performance issues, particularly within the menu interface.</p>\n<h2>Testing Live2D and Skepticism About Its Impact</h2>\n<p>The speaker plans to temporarily disable Live2D to assess its impact on the game&#x27;s performance, stating, &#x27;I&#x27;ll turn off Live2D, just to test.&#x27;</p>\n<p>However, the speaker expresses skepticism about the effectiveness of this change, noting that the game itself is resource-intensive and may not see significant improvement.</p>\n<h2>Expectations and Future Plans</h2>\n<p>The speaker acknowledges that the game is CPU-heavy and expresses a desire for better performance, stating, &#x27;Ideally... You know what?&#x27;</p>\n<p>They also express a commitment to resolving the issues, saying, &#x27;I&#x27;m gonna figure it out.&#x27; and express hope that the next beta release will be playable next week.</p>\n<p>However, they also acknowledge that the situation may not improve today, noting, &#x27;Maybe not today.&#x27;</p>\n<p>They express a desire for a better CPU to improve performance, stating, &#x27;Even a better CPU, it would run better, I feel.&#x27;</p>\n<p>Finally, the speaker notes that the settings may have reverted to their original state, which could be contributing to the performance issues.</p>\n<h2>記事情報</h2>\n<p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eJERBJql8O4</p>",
